# Line endings. Git for Windows checks out with core.autocrlf=true by default,
# which rewrites LF → CRLF in the working tree. That is harmless for files the
# host reads, but FATAL for the shell scripts that run inside the Linux
# devcontainer: `.devcontainer/entrypoint.sh` is COPYed into the image and used
# as the `app` service's ENTRYPOINT, so a CRLF copy makes the kernel look for an
# interpreter literally named `bash\r` and the container dies on start with
#   exec /usr/local/bin/devcontainer-entrypoint.sh: no such file or directory
# which surfaces in VS Code only as "An error occurred setting up the container"
# after `docker compose ... up -d app db inngest` exits 1.
#
# Pin every text file to LF in the working tree on ALL hosts. Windows editors
# (VS Code included) handle LF fine; the container requires it.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt and braces for the files that must be LF or the container won't boot.
*.sh text eol=lf
Dockerfile text eol=lf
*.yaml text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf

# Vendored third-party bundles: keep byte-identical (layout-base.js has mixed
# endings upstream), so `text=auto` above never renormalizes them.
.er_explorer/static/vendor/** -text

# Never touch binaries.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf binary
